{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElementBridge","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElementBridge","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.WenzlWeightVanishing","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.ColLenRowLensBridge","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SYTHookFormulaBetaProd"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElementBridge.schurElement_eq_schurPrincipal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElementBridge.schurElement_eq_schurPrincipal","kind":"theorem","line":267,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WenzlSchurElementBridge.lean#L267-L284","doc":"**The carrier bridge (unconditional).** For a weakly-decreasing, strictly\npositive partition `lam` and `Q ≠ 0`, the List-carrier `schurElement` at the\nprincipal specialisation `X = Q^r` equals the YoungDiagram-carrier\n`schurPrincipal`:\n\n`schurElement Q (Q^r) lam = schurPrincipal r Q (ofRowLens lam hl)`.\n\nThis is `schurElement_eq_schurPrincipal_of_hook` with the hook match B3 supplying\nthe hypothesis. It is the missing lemma connecting the two developments: the\ngeneral Macdonald hook telescope is proved on the YoungDiagram carrier\n(`QOU.SchurWeyl.sum_dim_wenzlWeight_eq_one`), and this equality transports it to\nthe List carrier. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElementBridge.hook_ofRowLens_eq_hookLength","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElementBridge.hook_ofRowLens_eq_hookLength","kind":"theorem","line":227,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WenzlSchurElementBridge.lean#L227-L265","doc":"**Hook match (B3).** For every cell `(i, j)` of `ofRowLens lam hl`\n(`j < (lam[i]?).getD 0`, `lam` weakly-decreasing and positive), the YoungDiagram\nhook length equals the List `hookLength`:\n\n`hook (ofRowLens lam hl) (i, j) = Partition.hookLength lam i j`.\n\nBoth are `(row_i − j) + leg`, where the arm is `row_i − j` and the leg is the\nnumber of rows below `i` still reaching column `j`. The YoungDiagram column\nlength is identified with the corpus list column length by\n`QOU.Mathlib.colLen_rowLens` (on `rowLens_ofRowLens_eq_self`), and the sorted-list\nleg identity `colLen l j = (i+1) + cnt (l.drop (i+1)) j`\n(`QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.colLen_eq_succ_add_cnt_drop`) supplies exactly the\n`hookLength` leg count `((lam.drop (i+1)).filter (· > j)).length`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElementBridge.schurElement_eq_schurPrincipal_of_hook","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElementBridge.schurElement_eq_schurPrincipal_of_hook","kind":"theorem","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WenzlSchurElementBridge.lean#L195-L225","doc":"**Assembly (B6), conditional on the hook match.** Given that the\nYoungDiagram hook length agrees with the List `hookLength` on every cell of\n`ofRowLens lam hl`, the two Schur elements coincide at the principal\nspecialisation `X = Q^r`:\n\n`schurElement Q (Q^r) lam = schurPrincipal r Q (ofRowLens lam hl)`.\n\nThe prefactors match by `nPart_ofRowLens_eq_nLambda`; the cell products match\nby `prod_cells_ofRowLens`, the content match (numerator, via\n`Q^r · Q^{c} = Q^{r+c}`, needs `Q ≠ 0`), and the hypothesis `hhook`\n(denominator). The single remaining ingredient for the *unconditional* bridge is\n`hhook` — i.e. `hook_ofRowLens_eq_hookLength` (B3, the sorted-list leg-length\nidentity). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElementBridge.nPart_ofRowLens_eq_nLambda","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElementBridge.nPart_ofRowLens_eq_nLambda","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WenzlSchurElementBridge.lean#L169-L193","doc":"**`nPart` match (B4).** `nPart (ofRowLens lam hl) = nLambda lam`. Reindex\n`∑ x ∈ cells, x.1` by rows: each row `i` contributes `∑_{j} i = i·(row length)`,\nand the total is `nLambda`'s `∑ i · λᵢ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElementBridge.list_range_foldl_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElementBridge.list_range_foldl_add","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WenzlSchurElementBridge.lean#L157-L167","doc":"Additive analog of `list_range_map_prod`: a left fold that accumulates\n`acc + f i` over `List.range n` is the `Finset.range n` sum. Used to identify\n`nLambda`'s fold with a Finset sum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElementBridge.prod_cells_ofRowLens","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElementBridge.prod_cells_ofRowLens","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WenzlSchurElementBridge.lean#L136-L155","doc":"**Product reindex (B5).** A product over the cells of `ofRowLens lam hl`\nequals the row-by-row double product over `range (length)` and\n`range ((lam[i]?).getD 0)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElementBridge.cells_ofRowLens_eq_biUnion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElementBridge.cells_ofRowLens_eq_biUnion","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WenzlSchurElementBridge.lean#L115-L134","doc":"**Cells of `ofRowLens` as a disjoint union of rows.** Each row `i < length`\ncontributes `{i} ×ˢ range(rowLenᵢ)`, and by `rowLen_ofRowLens_getD` the row\nlength is `(lam[i]?).getD 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElementBridge.schurElement_eq_finset_prod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElementBridge.schurElement_eq_finset_prod","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WenzlSchurElementBridge.lean#L97-L113","doc":"**`schurElement` as a Finset double product.** Restates the List-fold\n`schurElement` (via `schurElement_eq_prod`) as `Q^{n(λ)}` times a product over\nrows `i ∈ range (length)` of a product over cells `j ∈ range (row length)` of\n`cellFactor`. This is the shape that matches `schurPrincipal`'s `∏ x ∈ μ.cells`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElementBridge.list_range_map_prod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElementBridge.list_range_map_prod","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WenzlSchurElementBridge.lean#L86-L95","doc":"A finite product of `List.map` over `List.range n` is the `Finset.range n`\nproduct — the List↔Finset bridge used to move `schurElement`'s list folds onto\nthe Finset products `schurPrincipal` uses. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElementBridge.rowLen_ofRowLens_getD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElementBridge.rowLen_ofRowLens_getD","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WenzlSchurElementBridge.lean#L66-L84","doc":"**Row-length match.** The `i`-th row length of `ofRowLens lam hl` is the\n`i`-th list entry (`0` past the end) — `(ofRowLens lam hl).rowLen i = (lam[i]?).getD 0`.\nFor `i` in range this is Mathlib's `rowLen_ofRowLens`; past the end both sides are\n`0` (no cell `(i, 0)` exists, so the row length vanishes). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElementBridge.content_eq_cellContent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElementBridge.content_eq_cellContent","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WenzlSchurElementBridge.lean#L57-L64","doc":"**Content-carrier match.** The List-carrier cell content `cellContent i j =\nj − i` and the YoungDiagram-carrier `content (i, j) = j − i` are the same\nfunction of the cell coordinates — the first (and definitional) link between the\ntwo developments. ","signatureChunk":0}]}